Only UART backend changed in this commit: explicit file serial instead of nographic/stdin/stdout. Scout reproduced the timeout on b03d8e0 and the experiment with stdio, then saw both succeed with file UART. This supports a host/QEMU stdio-backend interaction, not a resident regression.

The test proves the emulated four-core Cortex-A53 noncoherent path: three secondary acknowledgements/SMPEN snapshots, refusal to release with SMPEN clear, plus relocated Rust pointer-table/FDT startup. It does NOT prove coherent release, hardware two-cluster bringup, SCM/ACC/L2 or eight-core handoff. No device operations.

Full kernel/image build, packaged-image inspection and host tests concern the identical production source/config at parent e204ec13a16b7f5926289e3f7ee72e83388c8c80; detailed reproducible evidence is in refs/notes/evidence on that commit. This commit changes only the test runner, not the boot image.
